1,11,'Mon-Tue-Wed-Thu-Fri-Sat-Sun 9:00 AM - 5:00 PM',0,0,0,NULL,'2026-06-10 10:07:53','2026-06-10 10:07:53',NULL,11,11,0,0,0,0,'tewt',NULL,0,NULL,'United States',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(11,1,'test','office','test','test','KS',111,11,11,'Mon-Tue-Wed-Thu-Fri-Sat-Sun 9:00 AM - 5:00 PM',0,0,0,NULL,'2026-06-10 10:08:55','2026-06-10 10:08:55',NULL,11,11,0,0,0,0,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'United States',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(12,1,'test','office','test','test','KS',111,11,11,'Mon-Tue-Wed-Thu-Fri-Sat-Sun 9:00 AM - 5:00 PM',0,0,0,NULL,'2026-06-10 10:08:56','2026-06-10 10:08:56',NULL,11,11,0,0,0,0,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'United States',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(13,1,'test','office','test','test','KS',111,11,11,'Mon-Tue-Wed-Thu-Fri-Sat-Sun 9:00 AM - 5:00 PM',0,0,0,NULL,'2026-06-10 10:08:57','2026-06-10 10:08:57',NULL,11,11,0,0,0,0,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'United States',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(27,1,'Testing Facility','retail','Carmel Village Phase 1, Calamba, 4027 Laguna, Philippines','test','AL',11,3,2,'Mon-Tue-Wed-Thu-Fri-Sat-Sun 9:00 AM - 5:00 PM',0,1,0,NULL,'2026-06-10 21:33:00','2026-06-10 21:33:00',NULL,2,2,1,1,0,0,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'United States',NULL,NULL,NULL,14.2048,121.118),(28,1,'Madison Square Garden','other','8TH Ave 31st St, New York, NY 10001, USA','New York','NY',10000,20,50000,'Mon-Tue-Wed-Thu-Fri-Sat-Sun 9:00 AM - 5:00 PM',1,1,1,NULL,'2026-06-12 02:45:03','2026-06-12 02:45:03',NULL,20,10,1,1,1,1,'Jalen Brunson',NULL,0,NULL,'United States',NULL,NULL,NULL,40.7505,-73.9934),(29,6205,'Freedom HR Solutions','office','625 N Valley View Blvd','Las Vegas','NV',2300,1,10,'Mon-Tue-Wed-Thu-Fri 9:00 AM - 5:00 PM; Sat-Sun Closed',1,0,0,NULL,'2026-07-06 17:23:28','2026-07-06 17:23:28',NULL,1,3,1,1,1,0,'Soleil Kline','{\"role_siteLead\":[{\"tier\":\"primary\",\"name\":\"Mickey Mouse\"}]}',0,NULL,'United States','FREEDOM HR SOLUTIONS\nData Security & PHI Handling Policy\nEffective Date: July 6, 2026\nOwner: Soleil Kline, Founder\nReview Cycle: Annually, or upon adoption of a new platform, AI tool, or subcontractor\n1. Purpose\nFreedom HR Solutions handles Protected Health Information (PHI) and other sensitive personal data on behalf of client organizations as part of benefits administration, HCM implementation, open enrollment, and ACA reporting engagements. This policy establishes the rules Freedom HR Solutions follows to protect that data — including how it is accessed, transmitted, stored, and handled by any AI tools used in the business — and sets a consistent standard regardless of which platform a given client uses.\n2. Scope\nThis policy applies to all client data handled by Freedom HR Solutions across every platform in active use, all communication channels used to transmit client data, any subcontractor or team member granted system access, and any AI or software tool used in delivering services — whether for drafting, research, training materials, or client communication.\nPlatforms currently in scope:\n•	ADP\n•	Paycom\n•	Paylocity\n•	UKG\n•	EASE\n•	Employee Navigator\n•	Flock\n•	BSwift\n3. Data Classification\nClient data handled by Freedom HR Solutions falls into three tiers:\n•	Tier 1 — PHI/Sensitive: Social Security numbers, dates of birth, health plan elections, dependent information, banking/ACH details, disability or medical accommodation records, 1095-C data.\n•	Tier 2 — Confidential business data: census files, rate sheets, org charts, unreleased plan designs, carrier negotiations, pricing agreements.\n•	Tier 3 — General/non-sensitive: publicly available plan summaries, marketing materials, generic training content.\nRule of thumb: if a document contains a name paired with a SSN, DOB, health election, or bank detail, treat it as Tier 1 regardless of which platform it came from.\n4. AI Tool Usage Policy\nFreedom HR Solutions uses AI tools (including Claude) for drafting, training material creation, and general business support. The following rule governs where that use stops:\nAI tools are never given direct access to platforms or files containing Tier 1 (PHI/sensitive) data. This includes not connecting AI tools to EASE, Employee Navigator, or any HCM/payroll system via login, API, or file upload where the file contains live client PHI.\nAI tools may be used for:\n•	Drafting training materials, decks, and guides using placeholder or de-identified data\n•	General process documentation, scope-of-services language, and internal templates\n•	Email and proposal copy that does not reference specific client PHI\n•	Research on platform features, ACA rules, or compliance requirements in the abstract\nAI tools are not used for:\n•	Uploading census files, enrollment data, or any file containing SSNs, DOBs, or banking details\n•	Connecting to client-specific instances of EASE, Employee Navigator, ADP, Paycom, Paylocity, UKG, Flock, or BSwift via credentials, MCP, or API integration\n•	Processing 1095-C data or other ACA filings containing real employee records\nWhen a client example is needed for training or marketing content, data is fictionalized or fully de-identified before it is used in any AI-assisted workflow.\n5. Platform Access Reference\nBaseline classification and AI-access rule by platform:\nPlatform	Typical Data Tier	AI Tool Access\nADP	Tier 1	Not permitted\nPaycom	Tier 1	Not permitted\nPaylocity	Tier 1	Not permitted\nUKG	Tier 1	Not permitted\nEASE	Tier 1	Not permitted\nEmployee Navigator	Tier 1	Not permitted\nFlock	Tier 1	Not permitted\nBSwift	Tier 1	Not permitted\n\n6. Data Transmission Standards\nWhen Tier 1 data must be shared with a client, carrier, or partner:\n•	Banking/ACH details are sent only as password-protected PDFs, with the password communicated through a separate channel (phone or separate email)\n•	Census and enrollment files are transmitted through the platform\'s native secure upload or a client\'s designated secure portal — never as unprotected email attachments\n•	Email is used only for Tier 2/3 content unless the file is encrypted or password-protected\n•	Verbal confirmation is used for one-time sensitive details (e.g., confirming a routing number) whenever practical\n7. Partner & Referral Data Sharing\nFreedom HR Solutions works with partner organizations including Champion Insurance, Custom HCM, Pursuit Pathways, and Haniel Business Consulting. Client data is shared with a partner only when:\n•	The client has been informed the partner is being engaged for a specific purpose (e.g., Champion Insurance for group benefits placement)\n•	Only the data necessary for that partner\'s specific task is shared — not full platform access\n•	The partner is bound by their own confidentiality/compliance obligations for the data type involved\n8. Subcontractor & Team Access\nFreedom HR Solutions currently operates as a solo practice with occasional project-based collaborators. If a subcontractor or team member is granted system access in the future:\n•	Access is scoped to the specific client group(s) they are working on, not blanket platform access\n•	Access is granted through the platform\'s own user-permission system where available, rather than shared logins\n•	This policy is reviewed with them before access is granted, with explicit sign-off on the AI tool restrictions in Section 4\n•	Access is revoked immediately at the end of the engagement or working relationship\n9. Retention & Disposal\n•	Tier 1 files are retained only as long as needed for the active engagement plus any applicable regulatory retention period (e.g., ACA recordkeeping requirements)\n•	Files no longer needed are deleted, not archived indefinitely, and deletion includes local downloads folders and email attachments, not just the primary storage location\n•	Password-protected PDFs containing banking details are deleted from local storage once the transaction they supported is confirmed complete\n10. Incident Response\nIf a data exposure or suspected breach occurs (e.g., a Tier 1 file sent to the wrong recipient, a lost device, unauthorized access):\n•	Stop further transmission and identify exactly what data and which individuals were affected\n•	Notify the affected client immediately with a factual account of what happened\n•	Determine whether the exposure triggers state or federal breach-notification obligations for the data type involved, consulting legal counsel if there\'s any doubt\n•	Document the incident and the corrective action taken, and update this policy if the incident reveals a gap\n11. Policy Review\nThis policy is reviewed annually and any time Freedom HR Solutions adopts a new platform, a new AI tool or integration, or brings on a subcontractor. Soleil Kline, as founder, is responsible for approving any changes.\nAcknowledged:\n_________________________________          Date: _______________\nSoleil Kline, Founder — Freedom HR Solutions\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(30,1,'TEST 1','government','123 Main St','Tondo','PA',2400,24,240,'Mon-Tue-Wed-Thu-Fri-Sat-Sun 9:00 AM - 5:00 PM',0,1,0,NULL,'2026-07-27 10:58:08','2026-07-27 10:58:08',NULL,2,4,1,1,0,0,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'United States',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
